§ `Article 1(2) -- extent (src:14-22)`

-- (b), (d), (e): England and Wales only
#ASSERT `art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 14` `England and Wales`
#ASSERT NOT (`art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 14` `Scotland`)
#ASSERT `art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 15` `England and Wales`
#ASSERT NOT (`art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 15` `Scotland`)
#ASSERT NOT (`art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 3, as to the Part III sums for attendance allowance, severe disablement allowance, age related addition and carer's allowance` `Scotland`)
#ASSERT `art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 3, as to the Part III sums for attendance allowance, severe disablement allowance, age related addition and carer's allowance` `England and Wales`
#ASSERT NOT (`art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 3, as to the Part IV increase for an adult dependant payable with severe disablement allowance` `Scotland`)
#ASSERT `art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 3, as to the Part IV increase for an adult dependant payable with severe disablement allowance` `England and Wales`
#ASSERT NOT (`art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 3, as to the Part V sums` `Scotland`)
#ASSERT `art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 3, as to the Part V sums` `England and Wales`
-- (a), (c): the dates for those provisions
#ASSERT NOT (`art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 1(3) and (5), as to the dates for the provisions in art 1(2)(b) to (e)` `Scotland`)
#ASSERT `art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 1(3) and (5), as to the dates for the provisions in art 1(2)(b) to (e)` `England and Wales`
#ASSERT NOT (`art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 7, as to the dates for the sums in art 1(2)(b)` `Scotland`)
#ASSERT `art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `art 7, as to the dates for the sums in art 1(2)(b)` `England and Wales`
-- everything else extends to both
#ASSERT `art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `any provision not listed in art 1(2)(a) to (e)` `Scotland`
#ASSERT `art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `any provision not listed in art 1(2)(a) to (e)` `England and Wales`

§ `Article 2 -- Interpretation (src:48-61)`

#ASSERT `art 2: the instrument that the short name means` `the Contributions and Benefits Act` EQUALS "the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992"
#ASSERT `art 2: the instrument that the short name means` `the Housing Benefit (SPC) Regulations` EQUALS "the Housing Benefit (Persons who have attained the qualifying age for state pension credit) Regulations 2006"
#ASSERT `art 2: the instrument that the short name means` `the Income Support Regulations` EQUALS "the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987"
#ASSERT `art 2: the instrument that the short name means` `the Universal Credit Regulations` EQUALS "the Universal Credit Regulations 2013"
